---
// Plain-language "who/what" statement placed right under the hero, kept as
// real visible text on purpose: the hero headline is a slogan, and search
// engines / AI answer engines lift a short, self-contained answer far more
// reliably than they infer one from marketing copy. Keep it ~30-60 words and
// in sync with the Person schema in BaseLayout.astro and public/llms.txt.
---

<section id="intro" class="intro" aria-label="About Doug Rosenberg in brief">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="intro__text">
      <strong>Doug Rosenberg</strong> is a Chicago-based jazz saxophonist, composer, and educator,
      with the debut album <em>Better Than TV</em> (2014), a New England Conservatory degree, and
      performances at Millennium Park, the Green Mill, and Symphony Center. He also designs and
      builds websites for musicians and small businesses.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  /* Left-aligned on the same edge as every section heading below it, and
     set as a lede (2026-10-25): centered, it was the one section breaking
     the page's left axis. */
  .intro__text {
    /* Wider and larger than the 44rem / 1.4rem it had (2026-11-01): the lede
       filled barely half the content width and left the right side empty. */
    max-width: 56rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.8vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .intro__text strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
